[["Map",1,2,39,40,47,48],"blog",["Map",3,4],"math-in-markdown",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":14,"filePath":15,"digest":16,"rendered":17},{"title":6,"description":7,"date":8,"tags":9,"category":10,"theme":12,"draft":13},"Beautiful Math in Markdown","Using KaTeX to render mathematical expressions in your blog posts",["Date","2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z"],[10,11],"Math","Markdown","math",false,"## Inline Math\n\nEinstein's famous equation: $E = mc^2$\n\n## Display Math\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{\\pi^2}{6}\n$$\n\n## The Quadratic Formula\n\nFor a quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$, the solutions are:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\n## Matrix Notation\n\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}\na & b \\\\\nc & d\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nMath renders beautifully with KaTeX right in your markdown.","src/content/blog/math-in-markdown.md","6eb59198c7b79c13",{"html":18,"metadata":19},"\u003Ch2 id=\"inline-math\">Inline Math\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Einstein’s famous equation: \u003Cspan class=\"katex\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex-mathml\">\u003Cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\u003Csemantics>\u003Cmrow>\u003Cmi>E\u003C/mi>\u003Cmo>=\u003C/mo>\u003Cmi>m\u003C/mi>\u003Cmsup>\u003Cmi>c\u003C/mi>\u003Cmn>2\u003C/mn>\u003C/msup>\u003C/mrow>\u003Cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E = mc^2\u003C/annotation>\u003C/semantics>\u003C/math>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cspan class=\"base\">\u003Cspan class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mrel\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"base\">\u003Cspan class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\">m\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mord\">\u003Cspan cl